Subject: winex11: zoom on a touchpad pinch

Wine reports touchpad input as pointer and wheel events only. A pinch
reaches the X server as an XInput2 gesture, which winex11 never selects, so
the gesture is dropped and Live has no zoom on a trackpad other than
Ctrl+scroll (issue 64).

Select XI_GesturePinchBegin, XI_GesturePinchUpdate and XI_GesturePinchEnd on
each top-level window, next to the touch events already selected there, and
report the scale change as Ctrl+wheel at the pointer. This is the input a
Windows precision touchpad produces for a pinch its application does not
handle itself, so applications that zoom on Ctrl+wheel need no change.

A whole wheel notch stands for a 1.1x scale change, but a pinch reports its
scale many times a second, so each report is worth a fraction of one and is
sent as that fraction: WHEEL_DELTA is a unit, not a minimum, and an
application that follows the amount rather than counting messages zooms
continuously instead of in steps. The running scale is tracked per XInput2
device rather than per event, so slow and fast pinches of the same size are
worth the same amount of wheel and two concurrent pinch sources do not
interleave updates against one baseline. WINE_X11_PINCH_ZOOM=notch rounds to
whole notches for an application that ignores the rest.

Ctrl is pressed once at gesture begin and held until gesture end, not around
every update: at gesture rate the press, wheel and release would each force
a wineserver round trip, and the application would see a real Ctrl key
down/up pair for every tick instead of one per gesture. The wheel updates
carry no modifier of their own and pick up MK_CONTROL from the held key. The
synthesized key is a left Ctrl, so an application querying VK_LCONTROL agrees
with MK_CONTROL. A Ctrl the user already holds is left alone, and at gesture
end the synthesized key is released only when no physical Ctrl is down,
checked with XQueryKeymap because GetAsyncKeyState cannot tell a synthesized
press from a physical one, so a pinch neither leaves Ctrl stuck nor clears a
physically held one. A begin that arrives while a synthesized Ctrl is still
held (a lost end) reuses it instead of pressing twice.

The wheel position is the pointer position frozen at gesture begin rather
than the pinch focal point: a precision touchpad pinch never moves the
cursor, but the focal point wanders with the fingers, and reporting it would
drag the cursor across the screen.

Gesture events need XInput2 version 2.4. The server refuses to select them
for a client that asked for less, so the version request only rises to 2.4
when the feature is wanted, and stays at 2.2 under WINE_X11_PINCH_ZOOM=off.
An X server without 2.4 warns and behaves as before. An unrecognized
WINE_X11_PINCH_ZOOM value warns once and disables the feature. Headers
without the gesture definitions compile the path out, with a warning when
the feature is asked for.

Depends on the send_wheel_input helper and the stdlib.h/string.h includes
from the middle-button drag patch.
